  "body": "Follow-up from #343 (per-setup browser tree).\n\n**Today (after #343):** a setup's Tool list node opens a table of the tools its operations use (number, size, op count, Edit) and offers the existing setup-sheet export, which carries each setup's tool list. A setup's Post node chooses the setup's own post, but the post OPTIONS (skip pauses and homes, one file per operation, threading output) stay document-wide.\n\n**What it should be:**\n- A dedicated \"Export tool list\" on the Tool list page (CSV / text: T number, name, size, kind, holder, ops using it) for the setup alone.\n- Post options per setup, following the document's until the setup's Post page sets its own (same own / follow-the-document law as the post itself), saved in the project file.\n\nDone means: the Tool list page exports the setup's tool list to a file through a command-free file write (like the setup sheet); post options round-trip per setup with undo; single-setup documents post byte-identically.\n",
